{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>And Ephraim</b> — I trained him from the beginning to bear the yoke of My commandments." "<b>And I passed over</b> — the rule upon every furrow: that I did good to her neck, and I joined Ephraim with Judah to plow." "<b>Jacob</b> — Jacob in his entirety, his field is his, by way of parable concerning the Torah and My commands. His sowing and his reaping is the recompense." "<b>Break up your fallow ground</b> — to remove the thorns, to clear the path, and it is time to seek HaShem, to water the seed; then the latter rain will come."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {1 "The syntax of the Hebrew is compressed; 'the rule upon every furrow' (החוק על כל חורש) is rendered hyper-literally as it stands."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:50.847489249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}